{
  "set": "mod-macro",
  "description": "MACROS \u2014 one knob, several parameters, which is the feature that makes a synth playable by an agent rather than merely configurable. A single 'Brightness' macro is routed to BOTH the filter cutoff and the resonance at different depths, so one number opens the filter and adds bite together, the way a real instrument's front-panel macro does. ONE axis: where that knob sits. The synth itself is identical in all four \u2014 cutoff 500 Hz, resonance 0.1 \u2014 and only the macro value changes.\n\nTwo things this demonstrates that nothing else here does: routing ONE source to MANY targets, and modulation of INSTRUMENT parameters (m39-b) rather than the mixer fader. A macro is also the one source that is position-INDEPENDENT \u2014 it holds its value with the transport stopped, which is exactly why it survived the anchor defect that made every LFO inert.",
  "variants": [
    {
      "name": "knob-at-0",
      "axis": "macro at 0 \u2014 the synth as configured: dark and tame",
      "commands": [
        {
          "command": "track.add",
          "params": {
            "name": "Lead",
            "kind": "instrument"
          },
          "as": "lead"
        },
        {
          "command": "track.setInstrument",
          "params": {
            "trackId": "$lead",
            "kind": "polySynth",
            "waveform": "saw",
            "attack": 0.01,
            "decay": 0.25,
            "sustain": 0.7,
            "release": 0.3,
            "cutoffHz": 500,
            "resonance": 0.1,
            "gain": 0.7,
            "unisonVoices": 4,
            "unisonDetuneCents": 10,
            "unisonStereoSpread": 0.5
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "mod.addSource",
          "params": {
            "trackId": "$lead",
            "kind": "macro",
            "name": "Brightness",
            "value": 0.0
          },
          "as": "knob"
        },
        {
          "command": "mod.addRoute",
          "params": {
            "trackId": "$lead",
            "sourceId": "$knob",
            "target": "instrumentParam",
            "paramName": "cutoffHz",
            "depth": 0.55
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "mod.addRoute",
          "params": {
            "trackId": "$lead",
            "sourceId": "$knob",
            "target": "instrumentParam",
            "paramName": "resonance",
            "depth": 0.35
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "clip.addMIDI",
          "params": {
            "trackId": "$lead",
            "atBeat": 0,
            "notes": [
              {
                "pitch": 36,
                "startBeat": 0,
                "lengthBeats": 1.5
              },
              {
